{
    "background_story": "Hana was a brilliant architect known for her innovative designs that often featured square shapes and clean lines. Growing up in a family of artists, she was encouraged to think outside the box, but Hana found solace in the symmetry and structure of squares. Her passion project was designing a community center for a small town, where she incorporated large square windows, angular roofs, and a central courtyard with a striking square fountain. The result was a breathtakingly modern building that became a hub for local activity. Hana's love for squares wasn't just aesthetic; she believed that the shape represented stability, equality, and balance \u2013 values she aimed to bring to every community she worked with. Her square designs became a hallmark of her career, earning her numerous awards and recognition in the architectural world.",
